                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played a lot of HOGs and I have to say I can't recommend this one.  First of all there aren't that many actual hidden object scenes, there are far more of the silhouette matching games.  I personally was not that big a fan of these silhouette games and felt there were too many of them, but even if you do enjoy them the fact that a message pops up asking if you want to skip a few moves into each of them gets annoying quickly.\n\nThe puzzles are also disappointing with many of them barely being puzzles at all.  Some of these \"puzzles\" include finding the combo to a safe elsewhere and then simply turning the dial to open the safe, another is a spinning globe that you just have to move a lens over the listed cities.\n\nI found the story confusing to follow and poorly translated with a lot of awkwardly worded dialogue.  I enjoyed a lot of the artwork for the various areas in the game, but on multiple occasions even though I knew the correct object to use to solve a problem I couldn't figure out where I needed to click to get it to actually work without using the hint button. \n\nOverall while this certainly isn't the worst HOG I've played I can't really recommend it, especially at full price.  It might be worth picking up at a discount if you are a big enough fan of the genre.",
